commits.message:
fix(ai-ui): show a colleague at work while the hand-off is in flight

@ag-ui/mastra buffers a server tool's TOOL_CALL_* and flushes them with the result, so during a message_agent ask the transcript carried no row at all — minutes of "Thinking …" while two agents played out a game — and the child's progress lines were dropped for want of a part to land on. The progress event now names its origin, the client opens the hand-off row on the first line instead of waiting for the buffered call, and the row shows the colleague's newest step until it answers. The chat lanes also resolve the space and the agent key before assembly, so a delegate reaches its Space and a leaf is no longer mistaken for one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

